---
// The review loop: a PR comment, sent to the agent in one key. Example data.
---
<section class="section rule" id="review">
  <div class="wrap grid">
    <div class="copy" data-reveal-group>
      <h2 class="h2">Read the review where you work.</h2>
      <p class="body"><span class="kbd">c</span> opens the whole pull request in the terminal: description, reviews, inline comments with their <code>file:line</code>, screenshots included. <strong>Send any comment to the agent in one click.</strong> It becomes a task, gets fixed locally, and comes back to you as the next push to allow.</p>
      <p class="body"><span class="kbd">f</span> does the same for a red CI: cairn fetches the failing steps' logs and hands them over.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="pr" data-pr>
      <div class="bar"><span class="lv">PR #418</span><span class="mu">Rate-limit the public API · 3 comments</span></div>
      <article class="cm">
        <header><span class="av" aria-hidden="true">M</span><b>maya</b><span class="mu">requested changes · 4 min ago</span></header>
        <p class="loc">middleware/ratelimit.go:42</p>
        <p>A fixed window lets a client burst 2× the limit at the boundary. Can we use a sliding window here?</p>
        <pre><span class="del">-  if b.count &gt;= b.limit &#123;</span>
<span class="add">+  if b.slidingCount(now) &gt;= b.limit &#123;</span></pre>
        <div class="act">
          <button type="button" class="send" data-send>
            <span class="lbl a">→ agent</span>
            <span class="lbl b">Sent to ENG-412</span>
          </button>
          <span class="note mu" data-note>The agent adds it as a task and fixes it locally.</span>
        </div>
      </article>
      <div class="task" aria-live="polite">
        <div class="tr"><span class="mu">── ENG-412 tasks</span><span class="ex">example data</span></div>
        <div class="t empty mu">No new task. Send the comment to give the agent one.</div>
        <div class="t added"><span class="warn">◐</span> Sliding window in ratelimit.go:42 <span class="mu">(from maya)</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-pr]");
  root?.querySelector("[data-send]")?.addEventListener("click", () => root.classList.toggle("sent"));
</script>

<style>
  .grid { display: grid; gap: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  @media (min-width: 1000px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(0, 0.9fr); align-items: center; } .copy { order: 2; } }
  .copy { display: grid; gap: 1.25rem; }
  .body code { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--fg); }

  .pr {
    border-radius: 14px; overflow: hidden; color: #e6e6ef; font: 400 0.86rem/1.6 var(--mono);
    border: 1px solid transparent; background: linear-gradient(var(--term), var(--term)) padding-box, var(--edge) border-box; box-shadow: var(--lift);
  }
  .bar { display: flex; gap: 1rem; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; padding: 0.9rem 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06); }
  .lv { color: var(--lavender); }
  .mu { color: var(--t-muted); }
  .warn { color: var(--amber); }
  .cm { padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem 1.25rem; display: grid; gap: 0.7rem; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .cm header { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; flex-wrap: wrap; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .cm p { margin: 0; color: #d8d9e3; }
  .av { width: 1.6rem; height: 1.6rem; border-radius: 50%; display: grid; place-items: center; font: 600 0.75rem/1 var(--sans); background: #35c1a0; color: #0c0d12; }
  .loc { font: 400 0.82rem/1 var(--mono); color: var(--lavender) !important; }
  pre { margin: 0; padding: 0.75rem 0.9rem; border-radius: 8px; background: #101117; font: 400 0.8rem/1.6 var(--mono); overflow-x: auto; }
  .del { color: #ff8f8f; }
  .add { color: #7df0a4; }
  .act { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.9rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .note { font: 400 0.85rem/1.4 var(--sans); }
  .send {
    position: relative; height: 2.1rem; min-width: 9.5rem; padding: 0 0.9rem; border: 0; border-radius: 6px; cursor: pointer;
    background: var(--lavender); color: #15161d; font: 600 0.82rem/1 var(--mono);
    transition: transform 160ms var(--ease-out), background-color 220ms ease;
  }
  .send:active { transform: scale(0.97); }
  .pr:not(.sent) .send { animation: nudge 3.2s ease-in-out 2s infinite; }
  @keyframes nudge { 0%, 78%, 100% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(189, 147, 249, 0.5); } 92% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 7px rgba(189, 147, 249, 0); } }
  .sent .added .warn { animation: beat 1.4s ease-in-out infinite; }
  @keyframes beat { 50% { opacity: 0.35; } }
  .lbl { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: grid; place-items: center; transition: opacity 200ms ease, filter 200ms ease, transform 260ms var(--ease-out); }
  .lbl.b { opacity: 0; filter: blur(3px); transform: translateY(6px); }
  .sent .send { background: var(--green); }
  .sent .lbl.a { opacity: 0; filter: blur(3px); transform: translateY(-6px); }
  .sent .lbl.b { opacity: 1; filter: none; transform: none; }
  .task { padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem 1.1rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06); display: grid; gap: 0.3rem; }
  .t { white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
  .t.empty { white-space: normal; }
  .tr { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; }
  .ex { color: var(--t-dim); font-size: 0.78rem; }
  .task { grid-template-areas: "h" "t"; }
  .tr { grid-area: h; }
  .t { grid-area: t; transition: opacity 220ms ease, transform 300ms var(--ease-out), filter 220ms ease; }
  .added { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(6px); filter: blur(3px); }
  .sent .added { opacity: 1; transform: none; filter: none; }
  .sent .empty { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(-6px); filter: blur(3px); }
</style>
